{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791582845,"nonce":"ANaNm8dbwCxiESlUKC66102CiXA=","message":"Measurement and inline runs landed: blinc_abi 2c89925 (text::measure, inline::layout), blinc_ts 3e5b1fa (measureText, layoutInline, Paragraph) and a baseline fix in the commit after it.\n\n**Measurement**: native.measureText(text, style, wrapWidth?) returns a TextMeasurement: lines (UTF-16 start, end, width), line height, ascender, descender, caret stops (index, x, line), caretAt(index) and caretNear(x, y). It shares blinc_abi's text::measure with the HashLink caret export, which now calls it.\n\n**Inline runs**: native.layoutInline(items, width, {align, breakWords}) over text runs (style, optional box padding), inline boxes (width, height, baseline, block) and breaks. Ported behaviour: whitespace collapsed across runs, greedy breaks at spaces, no space at a line's start, one baseline per line from each piece's half-leading plus ascender, left/center/right/justify (the last line and lines before a break are not justified; padded runs keep their spaces), long words broken only with breakWords, block boxes on their own line, max- and min-content widths. Paragraph realises a layout as non-wrapping text nodes under one node.\n\n**Baseline bug (user report)**: runs of different sizes sat up to a pixel apart. The layout's ascent was not the cause: the renderer puts a text node's baseline at exactly half-leading plus ascender, the same metrics inline::layout uses. The cause was rounding twice: pieces were positioned through layout, which rounds node positions to whole pixels, and drawing then rounds the baseline. Pieces now take their exact offset as a visual offset, which layout does not round. A pixel test draws seven runs (sizes 13-26, bold, italic, serif, monospace, line heights 1.2-2) alone, finds each baseline from its x's ink to a fraction of a pixel, and requires them within a pixel at scales 1 and 2; before the fix it failed (36.99-38.00), after it they agree within 0.02 px.\n\n**Left**: the host does not lay paragraphs out on its own yet (an element with text children flowing at its laid-out width needs a pass after layout, as a relayout hook); editing primitives (caret and selection as data, word and line movement, selection rects, scrolling the caret into view, IME composition in place and the caret rect for the input method).","files":null}]}